# How to cite this software. GitHub and Zenodo read this file.
# TO CONFIRM WITH THE LAB before the first public release:
#   - the authors (and their order and ORCIDs); the entry below is a placeholder,
#   - the licence (none has been chosen yet),
#   - the repository URL and a Zenodo DOI (added once the code is public).
# Please also cite the paper of each tool you use (listed under "references").
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the paper
  of each tool you used (MIPMLP, iMic, miMic, GIMIC, LOCATE).
type: software
title: "microplatform: the Louzoun lab's microbiome tools behind one interface"
abstract: >-
  A Python package (with a thin website) that profiles microbiome count
  tables, preprocesses them once with MIPMLP, recommends the right tool for
  the question and runs the authors' own code: miMic (differential abundance
  along the taxonomy tree), iMic (prediction from tree images), GIMIC
  (sample distances) and LOCATE (microbiome-metabolome links, in a validated
  Python 3.13 conversion). Every analysis also ends with a descriptive data
  overview (composition, diversity, sparsity).
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
authors:
  - name: "Prof. Yoram Louzoun's lab, Bar-Ilan University"  # placeholder: authors to be confirmed
keywords:
  - microbiome
  - 16S rRNA
  - preprocessing
  - differential abundance
  - machine learning
  - metabolomics
